    description: "Comprehensive ADHD testing and evaluation in Fredericksburg, VA. Expert neuropsychological assessment for children, teens, and adults. Evidence-based diagnosis and treatment recommendations.",
    heroSubhead: "Our comprehensive ADHD evaluation combines clinical interviews, standardized testing, and behavioral assessments to provide accurate diagnosis and personalized treatment recommendations. We serve children, adolescents, and adults throughout Fredericksburg, VA with evidence-based neuropsychological testing that addresses attention, executive function, and learning challenges.",
    introHeading: "What is ADHD Testing?",
    intro: ["ADHD (Attention-Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder) testing is a comprehensive neuropsychological evaluation designed to assess attention, concentration, impulse control, and executive functioning. This multi-faceted assessment goes beyond simple screening questionnaires to provide a thorough understanding of cognitive strengths and challenges. Our evaluation process includes clinical interviews with the individual and family members, standardized psychological tests, behavioral rating scales, and review of academic or work records. The goal is to determine whether symptoms meet diagnostic criteria for ADHD and to identify any co-occurring conditions that may impact treatment planning.","ADHD is one of the most commonly diagnosed neurodevelopmental conditions. However, it is frequently misunderstood and either over-diagnosed based on surface behaviors or under-diagnosed when symptoms present differently than stereotypes suggest. Many individuals with ADHD struggle for years with academic underachievement, workplace difficulties, relationship challenges, and low self-esteem before receiving an accurate diagnosis. Our testing helps distinguish ADHD from other conditions with similar symptoms—such as anxiety, depression, learning disabilities, or sleep disorders—ensuring that treatment addresses the root cause of difficulties.","The neuropsychological approach to ADHD testing examines not only attention and impulsivity but also working memory, processing speed, planning abilities, and emotional regulation. Research has consistently demonstrated that comprehensive assessment leads to more accurate diagnosis and better treatment outcomes. Our evidence-based evaluation provides the foundation for effective intervention, whether that includes behavioral strategies, educational accommodations, therapy, medication, or a combination of approaches tailored to each individual's unique profile."],
    signsHeading: "Common Signs That ADHD Testing May Be Needed",
